Akivot UI Workflow Realignment
Current Flow -> Desired Flow -> Screens to Merge / Remove

This document reframes the product strictly around the principles established in the chat history:

The product is not a management system.
The product is not a CRM.
The product should reduce pressure, not add it.
The user should understand what is happening without thinking.
The owner should feel calm and informed.
The walker should feel clear and operational.
Depth should exist only when needed.
The core experience should feel quiet, immediate, and almost invisible.
1. Core Diagnosis

The current UI is not primarily failing because of bad styling or missing components.

It is failing because the workflow still behaves like a software system the user must understand.

Today, the product often asks the user to:

interpret the structure
choose between multiple equally “primary” screens
navigate between entity pages
understand where actions live
remember where to go next
That is the opposite of the intended Akivot experience.

The target is not “more polished screens.”
The target is:

fewer decisions
fewer navigation branches
fewer conceptual jumps
more immediate certainty
one obvious next action
The redesign should therefore focus first on flow architecture, not visual decoration.

2. Product Model We Should Design For

Akivot should not feel like:

dashboard -> section -> entity -> action
records -> profiles -> billing objects -> management
Akivot should feel like:

open app -> know what is happening now
if action is needed -> do it immediately
if more detail is needed -> go one level deeper
if no action is needed -> leave with confidence
That means both roles need a strong primary screen.

For the owner:

“Is my dog okay?”
“What happened recently?”
“Do I need to do anything now?”
For the walker:

“What is next?”
“What do I do now?”
“Am I currently in a live walk?”
Everything else is secondary.

3. Owner Flow

3.1 Current Owner Flow

Current structure:

Sign up
Onboarding
Dashboard
Dogs page
Dog profile page
Billing page
Calendar page
Settings page
Current practical behavior:

The owner lands on a dashboard that already contains meaningful information.
But key actions are split elsewhere.
Dogs exist as a separate primary destination.
Dog profile becomes the place for deeper action.
Billing is also top-level.
Calendar is also top-level.
This creates a mental model like:

there are multiple “main places”
I need to know which one is for what
I may need to remember where a certain action lives
This is not aligned with the product principles.

Main problems in current owner flow

The dashboard is not fully trusted as the owner’s real home.
“Dogs” duplicates the same entity model already implied by the dashboard.
Assigning a walker is too deep in the structure.
Dog profile is overloaded with edit, media, history, stats, and assignment.
Calendar and billing are promoted too early to primary navigation.
The owner has to learn the app structure instead of simply being reassured.
3.2 Desired Owner Flow

The owner flow should be rebuilt around one primary home.

Primary owner question

Is my dog okay right now?
Owner Home should answer:

current status
last completed walk
latest note / signal
whether action is needed
one clear next action if something is missing
Desired owner structure

Open app
See dog status immediately
If dog setup is incomplete, see one clear action
If dog is active, see latest reality
If deeper detail is needed, expand into dog detail/history
If payment needs action, surface it contextually, not as a competing home
This means the owner home should become:

status-first
dog-centric
action-aware
calm
minimally branched
Owner home should include

selected dog or primary dog
live status if walk is happening
last completed walk summary
latest note if relevant
assigned walker state
setup alert if no walker is assigned
billing alert only if payment action is needed
quick switch only if multiple dogs exist
Owner home should not feel like

a general dashboard
a navigation hub
a control panel
a records system
It should feel like:

a calm “state of my dog” screen
3.3 Recommended Owner Information Hierarchy

Order should be:

Dog identity
Current status
Critical action needed now
Last walk summary
Recent history preview
Optional deeper detail
Not:

navigation
records
stats
profile management
action somewhere below
