3.6 Owner UX Corrections

What to change

Turn the dashboard into the single trusted home.
Surface “assign walker” directly from the owner home when missing.
Remove “Dogs” as a top-level default nav item, or demote it.
Reduce the dog profile page to a true secondary layer.
Move stats lower; they are not the first question the owner has.
Make billing contextual: “You have an open payment” rather than “here is a billing section.”
Calendar should be archive depth, not front-door navigation.
What to preserve

current status card direction
last walk summary
history preview
empty-state calmness
