4.5 Walker Interaction Corrections

Current issue
The dashboard card already says who is next, but tapping it opens a dog selection layer.

That weakens confidence.

Desired behavior

If one dog is clearly next, tapping should start directly or go to a minimal confirmation.
“Choose another dog” should be secondary, not default.
The interface should behave like it knows the work context.
Recommended walker start model

Primary CTA: Start next walk
Secondary link: Choose another dog
If there is only one assigned dog, no chooser should appear first
If there are many dogs and no clear ordering rule, then chooser is acceptable
But default should still feel decisive
4.6 Walker Live Experience

This is currently the strongest aligned part of the product.

Why it works:

one mode
one dominant state
visible elapsed time
clear finish action
good urgency escalation for long walks
low conceptual overhead
This should become the model for the rest of the app.

What to preserve

